-- title:
--   Theorem 2 — Algorithm 1 is well defined, stays in $\mathcal N$, and its accumulation points solve $\hat{\mathcal E}=0$
-- statement:
--   Assume the standing assumption of the paper and fix the parameters of Algorithm 1. Then:
--
--   1. Algorithm 1 is well defined and never stops: every iterate $w$ reachable from $(\hat\epsilon,X^0,y^0,Z^0)$ has $\hat{\mathcal E}(w)\neq0$, admits a direction satisfying $\Delta\epsilon=-\epsilon+\zeta(w)\hat\epsilon$ and (25), and for every such direction some $\ell\in\mathbb N$ passes the Armijo test; and from every starting point there is an infinite sequence generated by Algorithm 1;
--   2. every such sequence lies in $\mathcal N$;
--   3. every accumulation point $(\bar\epsilon,\bar X,\bar y,\bar Z)$ of such a sequence solves
--   $$\hat{\mathcal E}(\bar\epsilon,\bar X,\bar y,\bar Z)=0;$$
--   4. if the solution set of the KKT system (3) is nonempty and bounded, every such sequence has an accumulation point.
--
--   This is the global convergence theorem of the method; Theorem 3 starts from its accumulation points.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: $\mathbb S^n$, $\mathbb R^m$, $\mathbb X=\mathbb S^n\times\mathbb R^m\times\mathbb S^n$ with the trace inner product and Euclidean norms → `SymMat (Fin n)` (Frobenius inner product = trace inner product), `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m)`, `WithLp 2` products; reason: Lean convention; the same spaces, inner products and norms
--   - encoding: the standing assumption of p.2 (an optimal solution of (1) exists and Slater's condition holds), stated once for the whole paper → the explicit hypothesis `D.Standing`; reason: the paper assumes it throughout ("In this paper, we assume", p.2)
--   - encoding: "the infinite sequence generated by Algorithm 1" → any `w` with `IsRun D θ x0 w`: $w^0=(\hat\epsilon,x^0)$, and each step uses some direction satisfying $\Delta\epsilon=-\epsilon+\zeta\hat\epsilon$ and (25) and the smallest Armijo exponent; $\hat{\mathcal E}(w^k)\neq0$ for all $k$; reason: Algorithm 1 lets any direction meeting (25) be chosen; the statement covers every such choice
--   - reading: "Algorithm 1 is well-defined and generates an infinite sequence" → clause 1: at every reachable iterate $\hat{\mathcal E}\neq0$, an admissible direction exists and every admissible direction has a finite Armijo exponent; and a run exists from every starting point; reason: this is what well-definedness of each step (solvability of (24)–(25), finiteness of $\ell_k$, never meeting the stop test) means, as shown in Appendix H
--   - encoding: "accumulation point", "the solution set to the KKT system is nonempty and bounded" → `MapClusterPt w̄ atTop w`, `D.KKTSet.Nonempty ∧ Bornology.IsBounded D.KKTSet` in $\mathbb X$; reason: the standard cluster-point and boundedness notions for a sequence and a set in a normed space
-- source:
--   Liang, Sun & Toh, A Squared Smoothing Newton Method for Semidefinite Programming, arXiv:2303.05825v4, Theorem 2, p.15

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_HuberSNSDP_Algorithm

open scoped RealInnerProductSpace Topology
open Filter SunNLSDP.Equiv NonsmoothNewton.Shared

namespace HuberSNSDP

/-- Theorem 2, p.15 (Liang, Sun & Toh, arXiv:2303.05825v4).

Algorithm 1 is well-defined and generates an infinite sequence `{(εᵏ, Xᵏ, yᵏ, Zᵏ)} ⊆ 𝒩` with the
property that any accumulation point `(ε̄, X̄, ȳ, Z̄)` of it (it exists if the solution set to the
KKT system is nonempty and bounded) is a solution of `ℰ̂(ε, X, y, Z) = 0`.

The four clauses:
1. (well-defined, infinite) every iterate `w` reachable from `(ε̂, x⁰)` has `ℰ̂(w) ≠ 0`, admits an
   admissible direction, and for every admissible direction some `ℓ` passes the Armijo test; and
   from every `x⁰` there is an infinite run;
2. every run lies in `𝒩`;
3. every accumulation point `w̄` of a run solves `ℰ̂(w̄) = 0`;
4. if the KKT solution set is nonempty and bounded, every run has an accumulation point. -/
theorem theorem_2 {n m : ℕ} (D : SDPData n m) (hD : D.Standing) (θ : Params) :
    (∀ x0 : XSpace n m,
      (∀ w, Relation.ReflTransGen (Step D θ) (start θ x0) w →
        D.Ehat θ.kp θ.kc w ≠ 0 ∧ (∃ Δ, Admissible D θ w Δ) ∧
          ∀ Δ, Admissible D θ w Δ → ∃ ℓ : ℕ, Armijo D θ w Δ ℓ) ∧
      ∃ w : ℕ → ISpace n m, IsRun D θ x0 w) ∧
    (∀ (x0 : XSpace n m) (w : ℕ → ISpace n m), IsRun D θ x0 w → ∀ k, w k ∈ NSet D θ) ∧
    (∀ (x0 : XSpace n m) (w : ℕ → ISpace n m), IsRun D θ x0 w →
      ∀ wbar : ISpace n m, MapClusterPt wbar atTop w → D.Ehat θ.kp θ.kc wbar = 0) ∧
    (D.KKTSet.Nonempty → Bornology.IsBounded D.KKTSet →
      ∀ (x0 : XSpace n m) (w : ℕ → ISpace n m), IsRun D θ x0 w →
        ∃ wbar : ISpace n m, MapClusterPt wbar atTop w) := by sorry

end HuberSNSDP
